From: OpenDisplay <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dfu: boot: resolve the active slot for a firmware_loader image

Zephyr's MCUboot DFU helper resolves which slot it is executing from by
comparing PM_ADDRESS against mcuboot_primary and mcuboot_secondary, and nothing
else. In MCUboot firmware-updater mode the SMP server runs from its own
`firmware_loader` partition, so it matches neither and the build stops at
"#error Missing partition definitions", with ACTIVE_SLOT_FLASH_AREA_ID
undeclared at every use site.

That makes the mode unusable: the loader cannot contain the DFU library it
exists to run. Partition Manager will not reconcile it either -- it requires
the loader to live in a partition named firmware_loader and rejects aliasing
that name onto mcuboot_secondary:

  Partition image 'firmware_loader' is a container with a span of one or more
  images, but has the same name of its image. Container partitions are not
  allowed to share the name of the image that defines it.

The sysbuild path a few lines above already carries an explicit
"TODO: Add firmware loader support", so this is a known gap rather than a
misconfiguration; this adds the equivalent arm to the legacy child/parent path.

NOTE THE COMPARISON OMITS PM_ADDRESS_OFFSET, unlike the two arms above it. That
offset is mcuboot_pad, which precedes mcuboot_primary_app only. The firmware
loader is not an MCUboot slot image and carries no pad, so PM_ADDRESS is its
partition address exactly -- measured on nRF52840, both 0xBB000. Subtracting the
pad compares 0xBAE00 against 0xBB000 and falls silently through to the #error.

The loader is permanent -- never swapped, reverted or confirmed -- so pointing
the active slot at its own flash area is inert. The point is that the
translation unit compiles, letting the loader write the PRIMARY slot.

Guarded on defined(PM_FIRMWARE_LOADER_ADDRESS), so every build without a
firmware loader is bit-for-bit unchanged.

Measured on nRF52840 (Seeed EN04, chained behind the Adafruit bootloader):
firmware-updater mode gives a 540 kB application slot against 368 kB for
dual-slot, which on this part is the difference between 35% headroom and 1.4%.

Apply:   cd ~/ncs/v3.3.1/zephyr && git apply <this file>
Revert:  cd ~/ncs/v3.3.1/zephyr && git checkout subsys/dfu/boot/mcuboot.c
---
--- a/subsys/dfu/boot/mcuboot.c
+++ b/subsys/dfu/boot/mcuboot.c
@@ -107,6 +107,26 @@
 	#define ACTIVE_SLOT_FLASH_AREA_ID	PM_MCUBOOT_PRIMARY_ID
 #elif (PM_ADDRESS - PM_ADDRESS_OFFSET) == PM_MCUBOOT_SECONDARY_ADDRESS
 	#define ACTIVE_SLOT_FLASH_AREA_ID	PM_MCUBOOT_SECONDARY_ID
+#elif defined(PM_FIRMWARE_LOADER_ADDRESS) && (PM_ADDRESS == PM_FIRMWARE_LOADER_ADDRESS)
+	/* Firmware-updater mode: this image is the permanent firmware loader, which lives
+	 * in its own partition rather than in either MCUboot slot. Without this arm it
+	 * matches neither address above and the build stops at the #error below, so the
+	 * loader cannot contain the DFU library it exists to run.
+	 *
+	 * COMPARED WITHOUT PM_ADDRESS_OFFSET, unlike the two arms above. That offset is
+	 * mcuboot_pad, which precedes mcuboot_primary_app only; the loader is not an
+	 * MCUboot slot image and carries no pad, so PM_ADDRESS is its partition address
+	 * exactly. Subtracting the pad here compares 0xBAE00 against 0xBB000 and silently
+	 * falls through to the #error.
+	 *
+	 * The loader is never swapped, reverted or confirmed, so naming its own flash area
+	 * as the active slot is inert; what this buys is that the file compiles and the
+	 * loader can write the PRIMARY slot.
+	 *
+	 * Legacy child/parent counterpart of the "TODO: Add firmware loader support" noted
+	 * on the sysbuild path above.
+	 */
+	#define ACTIVE_SLOT_FLASH_AREA_ID	PM_FIRMWARE_LOADER_ID
 #else
 	#error Missing partition definitions.
 #endif
